# Citation metadata: GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" box from this file, and
# Zenodo reads it when it archives a release. Update `version` and `date-released`
# at every release (and add the Zenodo `doi:` once the first archive exists).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyAT in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PyAT: Python Analysis Tool"
type: software
version: "3.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zakgm2/PyAT"
url: "https://github.com/zakgm2/PyAT"
abstract: >-
  PyAT (Python Analysis Tool) is a desktop application for loading, visualising and analysing
  lab recordings: fibre photometry (TDT), NIRS (Oxysoft), generic tabular data and EFNMR. It
  provides motion and photobleaching correction, dF/F, event-locked z-score PETH, FFT, AUC,
  peak finding and curve fitting, with splice and marker editing. Its computation lives in the
  companion package PhysicsLibrary (ZaksPhysicsLibrary on PyPI).
keywords:
  - fibre photometry
  - neuroscience
  - signal processing
  - dF/F
  - PETH
authors:
  - family-names: "Grand Maison"
    given-names: "Z."   # as in the app's APA citation; spell out if you prefer
    # affiliation: "Your university / lab"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
